   ROUTE MANIFEST. If navigation targets a query string (navigate(`/checkout?planId=${id}`) with
   <Route path="/checkout">), read useSearchParams().get('planId') — useParams() returns {}
   because the route declares no :param. Only use useParams() when the route is path-parameterised
   (<Route path="/checkout/:id">). A mismatch fetches with an empty id, loads no data, and renders
   the error/empty state.

# UI QUALITY STANDARDS (PAGE and COMPONENT files only — skip for Java/config files)
1. LAYOUT WRAPPER: public Page.tsx wraps JSX in <Layout> from @/components/Layout. Admin*Page.tsx wraps in <AdminLayout> from @/components/AdminLayout. Never inline nav or sidebar inside a page.
2. SECTION CONTAINERS: <section className="py-16 px-4"><div className="max-w-7xl mx-auto">…</div></section> — content never touches viewport edge.
3. RESPONSIVE GRIDS: grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 — never fixed column counts on mobile.
4. RESPONSIVE TYPOGRAPHY: hero h1 = text-4xl md:text-6xl font-bold; section headings = text-2xl md:text-3xl font-semibold.
5. HERO SECTIONS: relative h-[500px] md:h-[600px] bg-cover bg-center flex items-center justify-center + <div className="absolute inset-0 bg-black bg-opacity-50" /> overlay.
6. HOVER/TRANSITIONS: every clickable element has hover: class + transition-all duration-200.
7. LOADING STATES: data-fetching components render a skeleton or spinner while isLoading is true — never an empty container.
8. EMPTY STATES: when a list/result is empty, render a styled empty-state with icon + message — not a blank section.
9. DYNAMIC COPY ONLY: business name, phone, address, hours — all from props or API response. Zero hardcoded strings in JSX.
10. MOBILE NAV: a Header/navbar that hides its links with `hidden md:flex` MUST provide a mobile fallback — a hamburger button (lucide-react Menu/X, shown `md:hidden`) that toggles a dropdown listing the same links plus the auth actions. Without it, mobile visitors see only the logo and cannot navigate.
11. TEST HOOKS (data-testid): put a `data-testid` on every element an automated flow must find — so browser e2e tests locate elements by a stable id, not brittle text. Use kebab-case with a stable convention: nav links `nav-<routeKey>` (nav-memberships); a form `<entity>-form`; its inputs `<entity>-<field>` (login-email, login-password, trial-name); its submit `<entity>-submit` (login-submit); primary CTAs `<action>-cta` (join-cta, book-cta); repeated list/card items `<entity>-card` (same testid on each — tests select by index). Add them to real interactive elements only (inputs, buttons, links, cards); never to layout wrappers. This is additive — it never changes rendered output or replaces accessibility roles/labels.

